  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've verified your account, Isaac, and refunded order K-6401 in full.\n\nThe delivery record shows the courier picked up your Kaze Sushi order at 6:25 PM and then abandoned it at 7:02 PM, so it was never delivered. I'm sorry about that.\n\n**What I did:**\n- **Refund:** $48.99, the full amount you were charged, including the food, fees and tip\n- **Card:** Visa ending in 4242\n- **Timing:** It should show up in 3\u20135 business days.\n- **Refund ID:** RF-4000\n\nYou may also see a second $48.99 entry on your statement. That's a temporary hold from when you placed the order, and it was already cancelled when the actual charge went through. It isn't a second charge, and it will disappear within 1\u20133 business days."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks. My order number is 6401, not K-6401, but I guess that's the same one. Is the $48.99 the full amount I was charged, including the tip?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, it's the same order. \"K-6401\" is just how our system writes order 6401. It's your Kaze Sushi order from 6:00 PM tonight, and the only recent order on your account.\n\nThe $48.99 refund covers everything you were charged:\n\n- Food: $40.00 (Dragon roll, 2 salmon nigiri, edamame, 2 miso soups)\n- Delivery fee: $2.99\n- Service fee: $3.00\n- Tip: $3.00\n- **Total: $48.99**\n\nThat matches the single $48.99 charge on your Visa ending in 4242, so you'll get every cent back, tip included."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, that works. Math checks out: 40 + 2.99 + 3 + 3 = 48.99. Thanks for sorting it out."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "You're welcome, Isaac. Sorry again that your dinner never arrived. The $48.99 should be back on your Visa within 3\u20135 business days. If it hasn't shown up by then, just contact us and mention refund ID RF-4000. I hope your next order goes smoothly!"
  }
